## Build the Compute Image

The OpenHPC components are installed into the compute image the xCAT-native way:
the osimage's `otherpkglist` names the extra packages and `otherpkgdir` names the
repositories that provide them, and `genimage` installs them in the same pass as
the base OS -- with the copycds base repositories in context, so dependencies
resolve. `${CHROOT}` names the image directory and is used by the customization
steps later in this guide.

`genimage` builds the image with `gpgcheck=0` for every repository (base and
extra alike), so the OpenHPC packages -- though signed -- are not
signature-verified at build time, consistent with how xCAT builds the base
image. Sites requiring verification should install OpenHPC on the booted nodes
instead (see the stateful recipe) or patch xCAT's `genimage`.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Register OpenHPC components as otherpkgs on the osimage -->
```bash
# Save chroot location for the compute image
CHROOT=$(lsdef -t osimage -o ${xcat_osimage} \
    -i rootimgdir | awk -F= '/rootimgdir/{print $2}')/rootimg/
export CHROOT

# Seed the head node's account database into the image before it is built, so the
# service accounts that genimage creates during the build (munge, slurm) receive
# the same UIDs and GIDs as the head. Without this munge is given an image-local
# UID, and when the boot-time synclist installs the head's credentials its
# on-disk state is left orphaned and munged fails to start.
mkdir -p ${CHROOT}/etc
cp /etc/passwd /etc/group ${CHROOT}/etc

# Extra repositories for the image build: OpenHPC, EPEL, and CRB. The base OS
# repositories come from the copycds tree automatically; these are added as
# comma-separated URLs, each enabled during the build.
chdef -t osimage ${xcat_osimage} otherpkgdir=\
"{{ ohpc_repo_server }}/OpenHPC/{{ ohpc_version_tree }}/{{ ostree }}/,\
{{ epel_base_url }}{{ distro_version }}/Everything/{{ arch }}/,\
{{ distro_base_url }}{{ distro_version }}/CRB/{{ arch }}/os/"

# OpenHPC packages to add on top of the base OS image
mkdir -p /install/custom/netboot/{{ distro }}
cat > /install/custom/netboot/{{ distro }}/ohpc.otherpkgs.pkglist << 'EOF'
ohpc-base-compute
ohpc-slurm-client
lmod-ohpc
chrony
EOF
chdef -t osimage ${xcat_osimage} \
    otherpkglist=/install/custom/netboot/{{ distro }}/ohpc.otherpkgs.pkglist
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

Build the image. `genimage` installs the base OS and the OpenHPC components
together and builds the netboot initrd:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Build the compute image (base OS + OpenHPC in one pass) -->
```bash
genimage ${xcat_osimage}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
